" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7573ddef-f834-5ca7-911d-588bad3a2d0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-65307" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain of the function is all real numbers.\n\n- **II.** $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n\n- **III.** The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The domain of the function is all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi $, such as $0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,….$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n,$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is false.\n\n- The graph of the function doesn't intersect the $y$-axis, as $x=0$ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c29a3814-a545-563e-9080-6c788b49451b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438356} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f89c4d-da0d-58fc-ab37-efc5ed7f1053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c29a3814-a545-563e-9080-6c788b49451b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438356} :answer-field/id #uuid "30435fb6-1037-57a8-b967-d652cdf699a7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0ebde88-a46b-560f-9b2d-c9311641fa24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438358} {:answer/id #uuid "d06a8128-c2a1-53e6-bd78-9b4f1b872f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d06a8128-c2a1-53e6-bd78-9b4f1b872f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438359} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa49081-1dec-5a36-ad7e-37cc67073211" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70935825-1eb9-59f1-b836-2b74b2e4e965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438360} {:answer/id #uuid "d95548b2-40ec-5ebf-b1ab-d29936ab04f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70935825-1eb9-59f1-b836-2b74b2e4e965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438360} :answer-field/id #uuid "168eb318-5e34-58b3-8153-3564c073e9ff" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69d68c82-75d2-569e-bc5a-a35be8a71a62" :question/math-academy-id "q-65308" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The range of the function is all real numbers.\n- **II.** $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$\n- **III.** $x=5\\pi $ is in the domain of the function." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi ,$ so $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$ Substituing $n=1,$ we get $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\pi ).$ Hence, Statement II is true.\n\n- The function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is defined for all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi ,$ so $5\\pi $ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1d4299d-351a-5fe9-a670-073cc9e5de38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438368} {:answer/id #uuid "fa255a93-20e8-54e8-97be-3ba846492184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa255a93-20e8-54e8-97be-3ba846492184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438369} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f1aeed1-5d5d-55f5-b47f-ad533ff3c9e9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98321251-a137-534c-9fe9-52d7da6b8d72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438370} {:answer/id #uuid "9af520a8-05f9-5db2-8313-3ee23294d164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9af520a8-05f9-5db2-8313-3ee23294d164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438371} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba5de37a-efe1-5701-9c49-2975bdd66304" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439214} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ea6006-9ee8-51ed-af73-840f5ecd72e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438372} {:answer/id #uuid "5b63ac11-cd0e-537a-9f3c-14ff4d9d34c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b63ac11-cd0e-537a-9f3c-14ff4d9d34c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438373} :answer-field/id #uuid "938f0d88-c3f0-572a-a97c-94e4a874dfb3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2712841f-ac1b-5d69-a817-019e60c121da" :question/math-academy-id "q-66483" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=1-x,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n- **II.** $x\\in (0,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-2,2)$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $-1$ and $y$-intercept $1,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/73/73d9277c040ae457ba6d96e162574edbeeef965d181fa6011ca4ab0e4644bd82.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ it is also invertible on $x\\in (0,\\infty )$ and $x\\in (-2,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124472 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd13aa5-83a8-5b23-96cb-ea665039ea30" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Invertible Function From Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b393ba9-a3ac-5808-94ed-3c11a65bce06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438390} {:answer/id #uuid "ce09f4bd-04c2-5f74-8906-b4202bebc260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce09f4bd-04c2-5f74-8906-b4202bebc260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438391} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf436ae2-cc85-573b-911c-97789c90dcfb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c0ee5d6-084d-56b8-aa0e-c0258d95d108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438392} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa5aec0-7411-557d-80cb-3019af06b156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c0ee5d6-084d-56b8-aa0e-c0258d95d108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438392} :answer-field/id #uuid "487367e2-2599-53c8-bf9e-30339ddec50f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439225} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c21a3f03-90d9-53cb-bb71-9eea038a85ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438394} {:answer/id #uuid "49438212-d7d2-5534-aa5d-01794d4a4385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49438212-d7d2-5534-aa5d-01794d4a4385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438395} :answer-field/id #uuid "05a53302-4e5d-5e14-b2b8-4f280d1ef98d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439226} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "375d71bb-fa6f-5e85-ae88-5ea752aa5bfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438396} {:answer/id #uuid "ab81d9da-3733-5304-9619-8e0a6d376495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438397}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "375d71bb-fa6f-5e85-ae88-5ea752aa5bfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438396} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbca9a6c-bf35-527a-b2dc-d52c66eea2c6" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0655d813-1b1b-5f2a-9217-33c596819669" :question/math-academy-id "q-66510" :question/problem "![](images/38/3897b7fcf079b2522cbd0138631a894cbca1005cd241524cf9f3995965278612.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/95/95b1bd18e41cba7d6d1175f66be053ffea52a32fbb35e2ad1d126dbeb2d73baf.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that: \n\n- For graphs I and III, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, graphs I and III show one-to-one functions. This means that these functions are invertible.\n\n- For graphs II and IV, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. So, these are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43d7d582-0e08-5fe3-8e62-df514f329d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438406} {:answer/id #uuid "41998fef-2e26-54fe-acf9-a5788490ab47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41998fef-2e26-54fe-acf9-a5788490ab47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438407} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0378409-4fc6-5ebd-a16b-b9ce526ffed5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439232} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd89e6d4-4284-5cef-ad54-c1065cbfd742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438408} {:answer/id #uuid "9f2c5391-3de3-59c1-a286-2ed065c30bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd89e6d4-4284-5cef-ad54-c1065cbfd742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438408} :answer-field/id #uuid "5868dcf2-b093-50db-b08d-7add6f5064eb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439233} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1e919a5-9466-584c-b9bd-7477e3370765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438410} {:answer/id #uuid "a16d2f7b-c0fb-5e81-8da1-26bc5ef53cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a16d2f7b-c0fb-5e81-8da1-26bc5ef53cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438411} :answer-field/id #uuid "d36afc1b-e6be-563c-8f1f-8a95a433bde4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26ae354c-e4a4-50d9-b820-8ba146650b10" :question/math-academy-id "q-66669" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(x-2)^{2},$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (2,\\infty )$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (-1,5)$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,2]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=(x-2)^{2},$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n1\\. Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n2\\. Translate it by $2$ units  to  the right  $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}.$\n\n![](images/1e/1e3ac550e35a3dc93b3e26e5834f763847b04f5133de02e368124f54dd2b9dd6.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-1,5).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/3e/3ebb316ca122b6786b8ef501fc7c56f8e0e68c8cfc32e5801c493d38382fc26c.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (2,\\infty )$  and $x\\in (-\\infty ,2].$  On these intervals, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/86/86c7c9cacc7a3868565f33130563ffed0ca423aa087e76cc08d103ea171822ed.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72a9977b-4906-5466-8a2e-080981fbbc3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438412} {:answer/id #uuid "bffb12a2-2512-535f-a05a-93d1ecd5edbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bffb12a2-2512-535f-a05a-93d1ecd5edbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438413} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cb31fe6-c55b-53f4-9367-7623acd76b6c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb16cbba-9564-553b-b9ec-711aa8dbca6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438414} {:answer/id #uuid "b93a4fce-89ce-58fb-80e2-43edf373bb3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b93a4fce-89ce-58fb-80e2-43edf373bb3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438415} :answer-field/id #uuid "6db6c671-dedf-53e0-be3f-fcd379f0e138" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439236} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b379a802-24be-59ce-b981-52720b5955d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438416} {:answer/id #uuid "c0459670-ed37-5d93-b901-b40e7e54aeca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b379a802-24be-59ce-b981-52720b5955d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438416} :answer-field/id #uuid "ade1d675-9ef4-50ee-b050-c20ae72bdedc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ffb9d3e2-6b9a-5fb3-b64e-0b7d921759d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-66679" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in (-1,3]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n1\\. Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n2\\. Translate it by $1$ units to the right,  to get $y=(x-1)^{2}.$\n\n3\\. Finally, translate $y=(x-1)^{2}$  by $2$ units down to get $f(x)=(x-1)^{2}-2.$\n\n![](images/f5/f53a4f97166877085c90acc01e3f8d0c6ac7bb3f704bbfb792d747122d314013.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/b0/b088c8ed1974a7c259dd54f85aec7a124579981971babfe8dee0313ca23b6458.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-1,3].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/b3/b3af13782a01213bb09fdeef38fbeb3fbca3f41348036e6786b4efa74a0166b4.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ff36d03-5cc0-5d73-83c4-e624a390bbc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438418} {:answer/id #uuid "530329fb-ce87-5e84-b072-5a38f2ebf633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "530329fb-ce87-5e84-b072-5a38f2ebf633" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438419} :answer-field/id #uuid "919e5c28-bbf2-5c80-b2d5-d434d820a43f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439238} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d13bb14f-1c20-5e94-8700-4dbd1f20f1b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438420} {:answer/id #uuid "78447fbd-2164-5eac-8c2b-44e4dc612b4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d13bb14f-1c20-5e94-8700-4dbd1f20f1b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438420} :answer-field/id #uuid "358639a5-54d9-573f-8827-054bd466e1e6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439239} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38e632a0-32b1-57b2-ba0b-ca870495c039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438422} {:answer/id #uuid "361ecb6e-6cba-52c2-866f-654d5b3bf821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38e632a0-32b1-57b2-ba0b-ca870495c039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438422} :answer-field/id #uuid "02fe17af-c7ed-530c-9d35-2b5a79dc67c3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1120070d-b929-5ac5-a6ba-244a40b57b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-66687" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+1,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,0]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-2,2]$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-2,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+1$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n- Reflect its graph across  the $x$-axis to get $y=-{x}^{2}.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=-{x}^{2}$  by $1$ unit up to  get $f(x)=-{x}^{2}+1.$\n\n![](images/83/83a9f5966c76b89b2cad9c6244e2e447fb0052fc7f946df954df76265628c4a7.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n*The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,0].$ On this interval, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/f6/f694b6b1bc979289b748758385e05575990bd866457e75a84fbf7bdf335c03b9.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-2,2].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once. Since  $(-2,2]$ is a subset of $(-2,\\infty )$, our function is not invertible on $x\\in (-2,\\infty )$ either.\n\n![](images/c0/c03118f3fd0193910b49e26ab5ea56e4320fd23583feb3267cd4442d0a157583.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cefd8d5e-1289-5ad1-914c-ab2775321488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438436} {:answer/id #uuid "b576a8c1-7ea3-5fa1-8acc-832863849d14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b576a8c1-7ea3-5fa1-8acc-832863849d14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438437} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ca5f16c-d2d5-56cb-9b50-6ad3cade9608" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439247} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "befc7759-bd31-5c8e-9555-3cb0dd101a77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438438} {:answer/id #uuid "43259996-4978-511c-985e-68d25446c510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43259996-4978-511c-985e-68d25446c510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438439} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c11a88-ed6a-52c6-9f46-d560f8833eee" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439248} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43a190ae-1ab7-5e97-aea2-ab2e9632fae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438440} {:answer/id #uuid "18ea5186-8355-5092-9c9e-79cb796117a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18ea5186-8355-5092-9c9e-79cb796117a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438441} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5a0d91-6853-5fb1-88df-fb42944cb144" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02e022db-b323-5e31-af64-39f79b6a6465" :question/math-academy-id "q-66725" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=-x+3,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (0.5,\\infty )$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in [-3,\\sqrt{2}]$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $-1$ and $y$-intercept $3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/aa/aaa05d1ab0fd630dacd81723fe00472cb901fb6f73af5f111f44459476191c0f.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ it is also invertible on  $x\\in (0.5,\\infty )$ and $x\\in [-3,\\sqrt{2}].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335904 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc2ebd76-b3da-51ec-9bb6-c0a8d8726a21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438442} {:answer/id #uuid "ed90097f-008e-5903-8afb-166e0fb732b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed90097f-008e-5903-8afb-166e0fb732b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438443} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb140f0c-688c-52f8-a90f-9018b950a280" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439250} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efd9c021-33f1-5537-af5a-c438ea2991ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438444} {:answer/id #uuid "4d46b3e2-aa3f-52ac-bda8-6b775f310423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d46b3e2-aa3f-52ac-bda8-6b775f310423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438445} :answer-field/id #uuid "5614c87c-6ed3-55e6-95b6-98e904f5c5d1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439251} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73ccc799-d970-5891-a63d-3482846a277e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438446} {:answer/id #uuid "52ff3f43-d7ba-5b03-a6cf-148b6c9c461e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73ccc799-d970-5891-a63d-3482846a277e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438446} :answer-field/id #uuid "404e5779-63f4-5bb6-b2a6-acf55f92288b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ee60b09-63e9-5076-abae-7337fc233de5" :question/math-academy-id "q-66729" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x-1|-2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,2]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-1|-2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n1\\. Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n2\\. Translate it by $1$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-1|.$\n\n3\\. Finally, translate $y=|x-1|$ by $2$ units down to get $f(x)=|x-1|-2.$\n\n![](images/75/753840da17642582f9dbc0debc18f1fa3efcbbb11142894c1dd823ad6c0c630a.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/15/15f1c797cbddd2ac8e2e9c5be72f842e7d1accfc5f619af57b1f35a27e1015c0.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,2].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/a1/a100489b49da7b06c98783b1b1c4ec0de9d891fc2b22f4b36b1a0ac2d54fc4f3.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e58af68f-eae1-53c6-9223-c7c0080b2c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438448} {:answer/id #uuid "5371e2e8-a318-5761-84cf-2a344ab71943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e58af68f-eae1-53c6-9223-c7c0080b2c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438448} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aab5ce5-7c11-54ef-9873-01b2782d09cb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439253} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af8f6888-4ad1-59e7-bb89-aa5f77d9746f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438450} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb5ab9d-c02f-5f8d-ae8c-1482c9a4f08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeb5ab9d-c02f-5f8d-ae8c-1482c9a4f08b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438451} :answer-field/id #uuid "5211022b-a915-5d40-8743-afe759a8dd9a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439254} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64cbf680-9981-52b0-97b5-fea787285feb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438452} {:answer/id #uuid "557bf5d6-ae71-5f3d-acc6-c84051652a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "557bf5d6-ae71-5f3d-acc6-c84051652a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438453} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac161744-e926-5973-8bfb-6bbc90ec7d60" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7aa0547e-3ef1-575a-ba36-cf93ffa1c8dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-66778" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x+1|-3,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- **II.** $x\\in [1,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x+1|-3$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $1$ units to the left,  to get $y=|x+1|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x+1|$ by $3$ units down to get $f(x)=|x+1|-3.$\n\n![](images/3b/3b9f56280089991c7db7652d84a777edd5c5e012921f0d48362f4fc3e4fd2a6e.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]$ and $x\\in [1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/fd/fd0b0fe70e009f43e80b0f712b6cfd576deb4c4c0457f61adae04cf7e44f140c.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,1].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/58/582ec1960b053731bf201c84d8c58fd4e1734a2b085cd5549a01aace4b600b4a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119784 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9d2a661-7d90-525c-9631-0c05ef108b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438454} {:answer/id #uuid "5deab4fd-cb30-5b98-a484-4483eb06b0c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9d2a661-7d90-525c-9631-0c05ef108b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438454} :answer-field/id #uuid "89c02379-086d-5617-b96e-c2e3ec7d9a9b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439256} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69513619-f7d9-5728-9237-83bd49e641c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438456} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7677e6-30d1-5eff-a3c5-95011127b77e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69513619-f7d9-5728-9237-83bd49e641c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438456} :answer-field/id #uuid "675400e7-a720-59bf-af25-ecd415319950" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63de0a7e-308e-5ca3-bfc3-0ba27b3a202e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438458} {:answer/id #uuid "179fafc0-1ae3-5917-a9f8-eae561e2b95b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "179fafc0-1ae3-5917-a9f8-eae561e2b95b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438459} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0b333bd-888b-5051-81d0-d4f153ba848c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439258}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "deb97145-eaf3-5dcc-a36b-24fae2c52b5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-68754" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $A$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** $A+{A}^{T}$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true, since the result of $A+{A}^{T}$ has all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\nA+{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087713 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7286fe-b6e2-5544-8bc6-86afc6cdb813" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Matrix by Its Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aec6ec60-6c46-5a6b-aae9-0f8a4513c381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438466} {:answer/id #uuid "fba8bd52-1ee7-5a66-a030-067347942322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aec6ec60-6c46-5a6b-aae9-0f8a4513c381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438466} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0fe543b-67a1-5453-9b3c-14bda0f7fe07" :answer-field/key "L" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5da5d9a2-db50-58af-8e1a-2040c4743955" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438468} {:answer/id #uuid "79c2e8d7-436a-562c-8bb6-320f546f60ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5da5d9a2-db50-58af-8e1a-2040c4743955" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438468} :answer-field/id #uuid "66bf24de-7a20-594d-b7de-c9ba0bf83e6a" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439263} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b03e3d6f-147f-5d24-9604-f561b464b7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438470} {:answer/id #uuid "7a1828d4-f877-5230-8b21-6196b52d43c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a1828d4-f877-5230-8b21-6196b52d43c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438471} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf585f09-cce7-592c-8c69-c352ff41bf81" :answer-field/key "N" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "166c18b6-0458-59df-a57a-4df3b7281df0" :question/math-academy-id "q-69518" :question/problem "Which of the following is a $3\\times 2$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,M=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,N=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $L$ has $2$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 2.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $M$ has $2$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $N$ has $3$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 2.$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, only $N$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087713 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed7286fe-b6e2-5544-8bc6-86afc6cdb813" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Matrix by Its Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59af6a9a-42c0-546b-9412-607e459cc142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438472} {:answer/id #uuid "cec8f887-19d9-52c5-979c-41bdf97dea66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cec8f887-19d9-52c5-979c-41bdf97dea66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438473} :answer-field/id #uuid "be4f58bf-8a1f-59a3-a571-f70e23545235" :answer-field/key "L" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439265} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "993a2e57-e68d-5c06-aff9-837e0885e386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438474} {:answer/id #uuid "bdba05ac-6cd1-5dae-b2b3-608524069bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "993a2e57-e68d-5c06-aff9-837e0885e386" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438474} :answer-field/id #uuid "79a8988a-9154-5b76-8c2d-70060f4d8200" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439266} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27f3b618-f6c1-5133-b95f-4d62f222ef52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438476} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e8aab7-25a1-50d2-a298-ab4532a330eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27f3b618-f6c1-5133-b95f-4d62f222ef52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438476} :answer-field/id #uuid "57f6da9b-4fb0-58b2-a7a1-8f738e5d1f4c" :answer-field/key "N" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439267}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c563e57f-2913-5048-b8da-281d6ade0aee" :question/math-academy-id "q-69523" :question/problem "Which of the following is a $4\\times 3$ matrix?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,M=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & \\sqrt{2} & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,N=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $L$ has $4$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $4\\times 3.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $M$ has $3$ rows and $4$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 4.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $N$ has $2$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, only $L$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89dca9db-88dc-5f58-9f23-ec98ca1bbc75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438478} {:answer/id #uuid "128f9548-3706-5b6d-94e4-afd0ea31e354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "128f9548-3706-5b6d-94e4-afd0ea31e354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438479} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8abcdf3-f784-54de-90bb-b51f314f8912" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439268} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b74bddc-ad74-5f61-a0ce-c1bb3f545d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438480} {:answer/id #uuid "f99619dc-7a17-50df-b37c-d5f5007df859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b74bddc-ad74-5f61-a0ce-c1bb3f545d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438480} :answer-field/id #uuid "96b81975-4ed5-5bfd-b978-ee8fdac7cf77" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad1a88c7-0f27-56c5-b163-10cc23842fb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438482} {:answer/id #uuid "97a592ec-ef1e-56af-8795-1ae139a9168a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97a592ec-ef1e-56af-8795-1ae139a9168a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438483} :answer-field/id #uuid "92e3b518-970c-5ddb-8ddd-c289c427c026" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "924829bc-4eac-54c3-82c8-f773955ca97e" :question/math-academy-id "q-69834" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $M$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $M$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $det(M)=1$\n- **III.** $det(M)=0$\n\n \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-4-12)+2(-2+6)+1(4+4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-16)+2\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =-16+8+8 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(M)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}]}
